Darwin: a target only read by framebuffer fetch is preloaded only while it is valid, in a Metal process.

A34 (local to this port; nothing here goes upstream). Patch 0017 adds the targets a fragment shader
reads by framebuffer fetch to batch->read, and panfrost_batch_to_fb_info preloads every target in
batch->read whatever its validity. In a process drawing through Metal such a target is now
preloaded only while its level is valid as well. What is not valid was never drawn, or its old
contents were let go by a DontCare load action (redwood_pan_forget, patch 0018): CoreAnimation's
second colour attachment, which it loads with DontCare and draws and reads back within one pass,
was read back in full for every screen-sized drawable pass in boot 0975-modes120-a -- and with a
kept clear in the same batch that preload ran over the whole screen (ALWAYS). A batch that
continues a pass cut short still preloads it: the batch before it made the level valid when it
was submitted.

--- a/src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_job.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_job.c
@@ -793,10 +793,17 @@
       fb->rts[i].view = &rts[i];
 
       /* Preload if the RT is read or updated */
+      bool valid = BITSET_TEST(prsrc->valid.data, fb->rts[i].view->first_level);
+      /* A34 (patch 0020): in a process drawing through Metal, a target the batch only READS (a
+       * fragment shader's framebuffer fetch, patch 0017) is preloaded only while its level is
+       * valid too. What is not valid was never drawn, or its old contents were let go by a
+       * DontCare load (redwood_pan_forget, 0018): CoreAnimation's second attachment, which it
+       * loads with DontCare and draws and reads within one pass, was read back in full -- a
+       * whole screen for every drawable pass (boot 0975-modes120-a). A batch that continues a
+       * pass cut short still preloads it: the batch before it made the level valid. */
       if (!(batch->clear & mask) &&
-          ((batch->read & mask) ||
-           ((batch->draws & mask) &&
-            BITSET_TEST(prsrc->valid.data, fb->rts[i].view->first_level))))
+          (((batch->read & mask) && (valid || !redwood_pan_metal)) ||
+           ((batch->draws & mask) && valid)))
          fb->rts[i].preload = true;
    }
 
